    motor: 'Tread Vision belt: 59 by 20 inches. Tread+ belt: 67 by 20 inches, described as 59 rubberized slats across that length. Width stays 20 inches. Incline is 0 to 12.5 percent in 0.5 percent steps on the Tread Vision, and 0 to 15 percent in 0.05 percent steps on the Tread+. Speed matches at 0 to 12.5 mph in 0.1 mph steps. Both want a dedicated grounded circuit of 15 amps or more, without a stated voltage.',
    warranty: 'Warranty length is not in the spec, delivery, or user-requirement lines transcribed for either Peloton.',
    verdict: 'Choose the Tread Vision for the 68 by 33 inch body, the 8 inch step-up, and 316 pounds, with the user-plus-20 ceiling rule and the large published clearances. Choose the Tread+ Vision for the 67 inch slat belt and 15 percent incline, and plan on 70 inches of height, an 11 inch step-up, 460 pounds, and user height plus 24 inches. If the rider is over 300 pounds or outside 4 feet 11 inches to 6 feet 4 inches, neither published range fits.',
